{"_id":"68f9e041166b018f83dfb4b9","roadmapSlug":"swift-ui","nodeId":"thS85PP8famziViKq49Tq","description":"# Structures & Classes\n\nStructures and classes are fundamental building blocks in Swift for creating custom data types. They allow you to group related variables (properties) and functions (methods) into a single, reusable unit. Structures are value types, meaning they are copied when passed around, while classes are reference types, meaning they share a single instance in memory. This difference impacts how data is modified and shared within your application.","resources":[{"type":"official","title":"Structures & Classes","url":"https://docs.swift.org/swift-book/documentation/the-swift-programming-language/classesandstructures","_id":"6a7f4ec1cb44947debd16302"},{"type":"official","title":"Choosing Between Structures and Classes","url":"https://developer.apple.com/documentation/swift/choosing-between-structures-and-classes","_id":"6a7f4ec1cb44947debd16303"},{"type":"article","title":"Class vs Struct in swift","url":"https://medium.com/@muhammad.cse11/class-vs-struct-in-swift-dcc7ad6f5a99","_id":"6a7f4ec1cb44947debd16304"},{"type":"video","title":"Introduction to Swift: Structs","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=d13uCPrmEXM","_id":"6a7f4ec1cb44947debd16305"},{"type":"video","title":"Introduction to Swift: Classes","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=s_x49coTM4g","_id":"6a7f4ec1cb44947debd16306"},{"type":"video","title":"Swift - Class vs. Struct Explained","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LtlbB4-6k_U","_id":"6a7f4ec1cb44947debd16307"}],"createdAt":"2025-10-23T07:58:57.990Z","updatedAt":"2026-08-14T17:22:09.974Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/swift-ui/content/thS85PP8famziViKq49Tq.md"}